-- title:
--   A non-strict section reduces to the prescribed crossing
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that becomes $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, the hypothesis `hj` that $j$ as a $q$-series lies in $\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, and a model $\mathfrak{X} :$ `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit, algebraically closed residue field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : R_p \to A$ compatible with $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $pb$ be a unit of $\mathbb{Z}/(M/p)$ represented by $p$, and let $\delta$ act on places of $\bar F = \mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,(\Gamma_N)$ through the diamond automorphism attached to a $\Gamma_0(M/p)$-lift of $pb$; let $SS$ be the finset of exactly those pairs $(s_1,s_2)$ with $s_2$ supersingular and $s_1$ its mod-$p$ Frobenius translate. Let $\theta$ be an $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphism of $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,M\,H$, $\alpha$ an integral $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra map from $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,(M/p)\,(\mathrm{infSubgroup})$ into it with $\beta = \theta \circ \alpha$ integral and $\alpha$ the identity on underlying Laurent series, $Psp$ a `JHPlaceSpecialization`, and $Rpd$ a prolongation datum for $Psp$ and $\theta$; assume the $\theta$-equivariance property `hwgen` for points of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}$, the dichotomy `TypeDichotomy` for $(\alpha,\beta,\delta)$, that $Rpd$ `IsModel` for $(\alpha,\beta,\delta)$, and the two compatibility families `hcompat`, `hcompat'` identifying, for $i \in \{0,1\}$, the place of a closed point of the fibre component $i$ with $\mathrm{reduceFst}(W)$, resp. $\mathrm{reduceSnd}(W)$, resp. their Frobenius relations. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\rho_O : R_p \to O$, maximal ideal generated by $p$, a surjection $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ and maps $jO : O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $\iota_A : O \to A$ compatible with $\rho$, $\rho_O$ and the residue map. Let $n$ be a point of the pullback of the two component maps $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,0$, $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,1$ with $(\mathrm{placeOn}_0\,n, \mathrm{placeOn}_1\,n)$ equal to an element $nd$ of $SS$, and let $W$ be a place of $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}\,M\,H$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Finally let $s_A : \operatorname{Spec} A \to \mathrm{XO}\,(\Gamma_M)\,hj\,\rho_O$ lie over $\operatorname{Spec} \iota_A$ and have generic point the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point attached to $W$ by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}^{-1}$, pushed into $\mathrm{XO}$; assume $\mathrm{reduceFst}\,\alpha\,W = nd_1$ and that $W$ satisfies neither `IsStrictFst` nor `IsStrictSnd`. Then the image of the closed point of $A$ under $s_A$ is the crossing point determined by $n$, namely the image of $n$ under $\mathrm{pullback.fst}$ followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,0$ followed by the base-change map $\mathrm{bcMap}\,(\Gamma_M)\,hj\,\rho_O\,\mathrm{to}\kappa$.
--
--   This is the geometric half of the node-matching step for $X_H(M)$ at a prime $p$ exactly dividing $M$: a section over the valuation ring whose generic place reduces to the first coordinate of a prescribed supersingular node pair, and which is strict on neither of the two components of the special fibre, must specialise to that node. It feeds the equivalence [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_section_through_crossing_iff_reduceFst_eq_and_not_isStrict_of_offDiag_of_surjective`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_section_through_crossing_iff_reduceFst_eq_and_not_isStrict_of_offDiag_of_surjective), where existence of such a section is characterised by the two non-strictness conditions together with the equality of places.
-- source:
